\pard\b\fs30 Chapter 1: The Observatory\b0\fs24\par
\pard In the quiet dusk atop Mount Hamilton, the brass dials of the celestial astrolabe began to hum with an unnatural resonance. Dr. Marcus Vance adjusted his spectacles, peering through the copper-rimmed eyepiece at the distortion forming near the constellation Cygnus.\par
\pard "The telemetry is impossible," whispered Elena, clutching a bundle of parchment notes. "These coordinates aren't mapping distance in light years\emdash they're calculating temporal displacement."\par
\pard Marcus tapped the mahogany desk. "Then the prototype is reacting to the harmonic convergence. Prepare the chronometer, calibrate the vacuum tubes, and lock the containment seals."\par
\page
\pard\b\fs30 Chapter 2: The Quantum Rift\b0\fs24\par
\pard A blinding flash of cobalt radiance engulfed the domed ceiling. Gravity seemed to hesitate for a heartbeat before inverting completely. The heavy volumes of astronomical charts floated weightless in the ionized air.\par
\pard Elena recorded their instrument readings swiftly:\par
