\pard "The event horizon is stabilizing," Marcus called out above the whistling turbine. "Whatever lies beyond the threshold of this century, we are about to step into tomorrow."\par
\page
\pard\b\fs30 Chapter 3: Arrival in Neo-Babylon\b0\fs24\par
\pard When Marcus opened his eyes, the obsidian floor under his boots vibrated with magnetic currents. Towers of crystalline quartz stretched into a copper-tinted twilight sky, laced with elevated transit skyways and illuminated hanging gardens.\par
\pard "We made it," whispered Elena, tracing the geometric light patterns pulsing along the architectural spires. "Two thousand years into antiquity, yet technologically centuries ahead of our own world."\par
\pard A distant mechanical chime echoed through the terrace. The chronometer clicked forward, and their uncharted journey had only just begun.\par
